{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>From the valley of Chevron.</b> But is Chevron not in the hill country, as it says, ״וַיַּעֲלוּ בַנֶּגֶב וַיָּבֹא עַד חֶבְרוֹן״ (Numbers 13)? Rather, from the deep counsel of that righteous one buried in Chevron — to fulfill what was said to Avraham between the pieces: ״כִּי גֵר יִהְיֶה זַרְעֲךָ״ (Genesis 15:13)." "<b>And he came to Shechem.</b> A place prepared for punishment: there the tribes corrupted themselves, there they abused Dinah, there the kingdom of the House of David was split, as it says, ״וַיֵּלֶךְ רְחַבְעָם שְׁכֶמָה״ (I Kings 12)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:27.033892208Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}